{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court and McLaughlin Chiropractic Associates",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0000-0000",
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "McKesson\u2019s unsolicited fax advertisements to medical practices, including McLaughlin, gave rise to a TCPA lawsuit alleging violations of the required opt\u2011out notice."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0000-0002",
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "During the pending lawsuit, a company sought an FCC declaratory ruling on the applicability of the TCPA to online fax services, leading the FCC to issue the Amerifactors order excluding such services from the TCPA definition."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0000",
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0001",
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The legal question before the Court was whether the Hobbs Act bars district courts from reviewing the FCC\u2019s interpretation of the TCPA in enforcement proceedings."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "scotus-23-1226",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Section\u202f703 of the Administrative Procedure Act provides a default principle that parties in enforcement proceedings can challenge an agency\u2019s interpretation of a statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In enforcement proceedings, district courts independently determine whether an agency\u2019s interpretation of a statute is correct."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Hobbs Act does not bar McLaughlin from arguing in the district\u2011court enforcement proceeding that the FCC\u2019s interpretation of the TCPA is incorrect."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh dissented, stating that the Hobbs Act provides exclusive jurisdiction to the courts of appeals."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0002-0005",
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan dissented, arguing that \u201cexclusive\u201d means courts of appeals alone, not district courts, and citing Port of Boston Marine Terminal Assn. v. Rederiaktiebolaget Transatlantic, which forecloses a district court\u2019s collateral redetermination of an agency order."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Decision",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
