  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "McKesson Corporation sent unsolicited fax advertisements through a subsidiary in 2009 and 2010 to medical practices, including McLaughlin Chiropractic Associates."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "McLaughlin Chiropractic Associates",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to McLaughlin Chiropractic Associates, mcLaughlin sued McKesson in the U.S. District Court for the Northern District of California in 2014, alleging TCPA violations for faxing unsolicited advertisements without the required opt\u2011out notices."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "While the lawsuit was pending, a company petitioned the FCC for a declaratory ruling on whether the TCPA applies to faxes received through online fax services."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Months after class certification, the FCC issued the Amerifactors order, interpreting \u201ctelephone facsimile machine\u201d in the TCPA to exclude online fax services."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0000",
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that \u00a7\u202f703 of the Administrative Procedure Act provides a default principle that parties in enforcement proceedings can challenge an agency\u2019s interpretation of a statute, and that district courts may independently determine whether the agency\u2019s interpretation is correct."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority further held that the Hobbs Act does not bar McLaughlin from arguing in the district\u2011court enforcement proceeding that the FCC\u2019s interpretation of the TCPA is incorrect."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justices Kavanaugh and Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0001-0005",
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0002-0005",
              "ev-903dbe41e126-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justices Kavanaugh and Kagan dissented, arguing that the Hobbs Act provides exclusive jurisdiction to the courts of appeals, and citing precedent that bars district\u2011court \u201ccollateral redetermination\u201d of agency orders."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "McKesson and the Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "903dbe41e1267aaf125f2cbca1836df3b8ae0fc0fb76f6492613d2f9f145120f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-903dbe41e126-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "McKesson and the Government argue that practical problems could arise if the Hobbs Act did not bar judicial review of agency legal interpretations in enforcement proceedings."
        }
      ],
